---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: What's on
permalink: /whats-on/
heading: What's on in Largs
subtitle: Events in and around the town, every one checked before it goes up.
---
<section class="board wrap" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="kicker">
    <span class="stamp">Free to list · verified before publishing</span>
  </div>
  <p class="page-intro">Upcoming events in and around Largs — from the seafront
  to the stage. All listings are checked before they go up. Free to submit.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap whatson-section" aria-label="Upcoming events">

  {# Separate upcoming events into those with and without images #}
  {% set allEvents = events.items | upcoming %}

  {% if allEvents | length == 0 %}
  <p class="no-events">No upcoming events at the moment — check back soon,
  or <a href="mailto:events@largs.scot?subject=Event%20submission%20for%20Largs&body=Title%3A%0ADate%3A%0AVenue%3A%0ATime%3A%0ADescription%3A%0AWebsite%20or%20booking%20link%20(if%20any)%3A%0A%0AImage%20(optional)%3A%20Please%20attach%20a%20photo%20if%20you%20have%20one%20%E2%80%94%20your%20own%20photograph%20or%20one%20you%20have%20permission%20to%20use.%20A%20square%20image%20works%20best%2C%20600%20pixels%20or%20bigger%3B%20we%20crop%20it%20to%20fit.%20By%20attaching%20an%20image%20you%20confirm%20Largs%20may%20publish%20it%20alongside%20your%20event%20listing.">submit one</a>.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {# ONE LIST, IN DATE ORDER. There used to be a featured tier: any event
     carrying an image got a wide card above everything else, under its own
     subheading. Removed 30 Aug 2026, the day the first submitted image
     arrived and the effect could be seen for real.

     Two reasons. A list in date order is more useful — somebody checking
     what is on wants to know what is next, not read the top of the page and
     then start again below it. And an image is a proxy for whether an
     organiser has a designer, not for whether the event matters to the
     town: an eightieth anniversary concert sat below an artisan market
     because one organiser sent a poster. The submission email invites a
     photo without saying it buys top billing, so either the ask discloses
     that or the promotion goes.

     The wide card went too, on 31 Aug 2026. It kept the promotion in
     everything but position: a bordered panel among plain rows still reads
     as a featured item, and the only thing separating them was whether the
     organiser had a designer. An image is now capped at a fixed width and
     sits in its own column between the date and the words, so a picture
     adds information without conferring rank — the same answer the
     directory reached with its fixed 56px logo box. See .event-main in
     site.css for why it is a column rather than a float, and what that
     costs. #}
  <div class="event-list">
  {% for e in allEvents %}
  <article class="event">
    <div class="when">
      <div class="dow">{{ e.badgeTop }}</div>
      <div class="dom">{{ e.date | dom }}</div>{% if e.badgeYear %}<div class="yr">{{ e.badgeYear }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {# Date, then picture, then words. The image is a column here rather
       than a float at the right-hand edge: a reader working left to right
       meets it before the blurb, where at the far right it was simply not
       being looked at. A row with a picture therefore starts its text
       further right than one without — that unevenness was weighed against
       the picture being seen, and lost (31 Aug 2026).

       alt is empty on purpose: the title sits beside it as a heading and a
       poster's own words are already in the listing, so announcing them
       twice helps nobody. #}
    <div class="event-main">
      {% if e.image %}<img class="event-img" src="{{ e.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
      <div class="event-body">
        <h3>{{ e.title }}</h3>
        <div class="meta">{% if e.onNow %}<span class="on-now">On now</span> · {% endif %}{{ e.venue | upper }} · {{ e.time | upper }}</div>
        <p>{{ e.blurb }}</p>
        {% if e.url %}<a class="event-link" href="{{ e.url }}">More info →</a>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>

</section>

{# Event structured data. This is the one piece of markup on the site with
   a real chance of earning a rich result: events with valid Event schema
   can appear in Google's event listings for "what's on in largs", and
   nobody else marks up this town's events at all.

   Recomputed from events.items rather than reusing allEvents, so this
   block does not depend on a variable set elsewhere in the template.

   Only events with a title, a date and a venue are emitted: incomplete
   structured data is worse than none, because Google may distrust the
   page rather than merely ignore the item. The address is the town
   rather than a street -- venue names in Largs are unambiguous locally,
   and inventing a postcode we do not hold would be worse than omitting
   one. #}
{%- set schemaEvents = events.items | upcoming -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
[
{%- set comma = joiner(",") -%}
{%- for e in schemaEvents %}{% if e.title and e.date and e.venue %}{{ comma() }}
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event",
"name":{{ e.title | dump | safe }},
"startDate":"{{ e.date }}",
{% if e.until %}"endDate":"{{ e.until }}",{% endif %}
"eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled",
{% if e.blurb %}"description":{{ e.blurb | dump | safe }},{% endif %}
{% if e.url %}"url":{{ e.url | dump | safe }},{% endif %}
"location":{"@type":"Place","name":{{ e.venue | dump | safe }},"address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Largs","addressRegion":"North Ayrshire","addressCountry":"GB"}}}
{%- endif %}{% endfor %}
]
</script>

{% include "regulars.njk" %}

<section class="whatson-submit wrap" aria-labelledby="submit-h">
  <h2 id="submit-h">Add your event or class</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p>Listings are free. Send the details to
  <a href="mailto:events@largs.scot?subject=Event%20submission%20for%20Largs&body=Title%3A%0ADate%3A%0AVenue%3A%0ATime%3A%0ADescription%3A%0AWebsite%20or%20booking%20link%20(if%20any)%3A%0A%0AImage%20(optional)%3A%20Please%20attach%20a%20photo%20if%20you%20have%20one%20%E2%80%94%20your%20own%20photograph%20or%20one%20you%20have%20permission%20to%20use.%20A%20square%20image%20works%20best%2C%20600%20pixels%20or%20bigger%3B%20we%20crop%20it%20to%20fit.%20By%20attaching%20an%20image%20you%20confirm%20Largs%20may%20publish%20it%20alongside%20your%20event%20listing.">events@largs.scot</a>
  and we'll get it up within a day or two.</p>
  <ul class="submit-list">
    <li>Title, date, venue and time</li>
    <li>A sentence or two about the event</li>
    <li>A website or booking link if there is one</li>
    <li>A photo if you have one you own or have permission to use — square
    works best, 600 pixels or bigger, and we'll crop it to fit</li>
  </ul>
</section>

